# Summarisation references. Source passages and references written for this repository.
{"id": "sum-d01", "reference": "The transit authority is replacing its fare system over six months, withdrawing paper tickets and offering contactless cards at stations, with concessions carried over for registered riders.", "split": "dev", "text": "The transit authority will replace its fare system over six months. Paper tickets are withdrawn first, followed by the older magnetic cards. Riders without smartphones can collect contactless cards at any station. Concession fares carry over automatically for registered riders."}
{"id": "sum-d02", "reference": "Moving inspections from the end of the line to three mid-line checkpoints cut a plant's defect rate from four percent to just over one, without new equipment.", "split": "dev", "text": "A manufacturing plant cut its defect rate by moving inspections earlier. Previously every unit was checked at the end of the line. Three mid-line checkpoints replaced that single stage. Defects fell from four percent to just over one percent with no new equipment."}
{"id": "sum-d03", "reference": "From next month the library will close at nine on weekdays and open Sundays from noon to five, funded by a two-year grant that will be reviewed before expiry.", "split": "dev", "text": "The library is extending its opening hours from next month. Weekday closing moves from six to nine in the evening. Sunday opening is new, running from noon until five. A two-year grant funds the change and will be reviewed before it expires."}
{"id": "sum-d04", "reference": "A twelve-week study found three short daily exercise sessions produced markedly better adherence than one longer session, with comparable fitness gains.", "split": "dev", "text": "Researchers compared two exercise schedules over twelve weeks. One group did a single thirty-minute session daily. The other did three ten-minute sessions. Adherence was markedly higher in the shorter-session group while fitness gains were comparable."}
{"id": "sum-d05", "reference": "The council approved turning three car parks into gardens, budgeting four million, starting in March over eighteen months, with two hundred replacement spaces added to a garage.", "split": "dev", "text": "The council approved converting three car parks into public gardens. Work begins in March and should take eighteen months. Four million was allocated from the capital fund. Two hundred replacement spaces will be added to an existing garage."}
{"id": "sum-d06", "reference": "By rebuilding only changed services, a team cut median deployment time from ninety minutes to eleven, keeping nightly full rebuilds to catch integration problems.", "split": "dev", "text": "A software team reduced deployment time by rebuilding only what changed. The old pipeline rebuilt every service on each commit and took ninety minutes. Change detection brought the median down to eleven minutes. Full rebuilds still run nightly to catch integration problems."}
{"id": "sum-d07", "reference": "The university replaced its July housing lottery with questionnaire matching on sleep and study habits, halving reassignment requests but removing student choice.", "split": "dev", "text": "The university replaced its housing lottery with questionnaire-based matching. Students previously chose dormitories at random in July. The new process pairs them by sleep and study habits. Reassignment requests halved in trials, though some students disliked losing the choice."}
{"id": "sum-d08", "reference": "A hospital's telehealth clinic lets post-surgical patients attend two of three follow-ups by video, saving long journeys, while the final physical examination stays in person.", "split": "dev", "text": "A regional hospital opened a telehealth clinic for post-surgical follow-ups. Patients now attend two of three appointments by video. Rural patients who once drove three hours each way save the journey. The final appointment stays in person because it needs a physical examination."}
{"id": "sum-t01", "reference": "The water utility will replace lead service lines at around nine thousand properties in phases until 2030, starting with schools, notifying residents four weeks ahead.", "split": "test", "text": "The water utility will replace lead service lines across the old town. Around nine thousand properties are affected. Work runs in phases until 2030, starting with schools and nurseries. Residents will be notified four weeks before work reaches their street."}
{"id": "sum-t02", "reference": "A retailer halved average checkout waiting time by matching staff scheduling to measured footfall, with no change in staff costs because total hours stayed the same.", "split": "test", "text": "A retailer trialled shorter checkout queues by changing staff scheduling. Tills were previously staffed evenly through the day. Matching staff to measured footfall cut average waiting time by half. Staff costs were unchanged because total hours stayed the same."}
{"id": "sum-t03", "reference": "The museum spent two years digitising forty thousand photographic prints, with volunteers transcribing captions, producing a searchable catalogue that is free online.", "split": "test", "text": "The museum digitised its photographic archive over two years. Around forty thousand prints were scanned at high resolution. Volunteers transcribed the handwritten captions. The catalogue is now searchable and freely available online."}
{"id": "sum-t04", "reference": "A city's refundable deposit scheme for drink containers reached eighty percent return rates within a year and sharply reduced litter.", "split": "test", "text": "A city introduced a deposit scheme for drink containers. Shoppers pay a small deposit refunded on return. Return rates reached eighty percent within a year. Litter surveys recorded a sharp fall in discarded containers."}
{"id": "sum-t05", "reference": "An airline cut average gate time by seven minutes by boarding window seats first instead of by ticket class alone, and crew reported fewer aisle blockages.", "split": "test", "text": "The airline changed its boarding procedure to reduce delays. Passengers previously boarded by ticket class alone. Boarding by window seats first cut the average time at the gate by seven minutes. Crew reported fewer aisle blockages."}
{"id": "sum-t06", "reference": "A school moved older pupils' start time an hour later, improving first-lesson attendance and concentration, at the cost of reorganising bus scheduling.", "split": "test", "text": "A school moved its start time an hour later for older pupils. Attendance in first lessons improved noticeably. Teachers reported fewer late arrivals and better concentration. Bus scheduling had to be reorganised to make it work."}
{"id": "sum-t07", "reference": "New regulator rules require battery storage operators to file thermal management plans and observe minimum distances from housing, with two years for existing sites to comply.", "split": "test", "text": "The regulator published new rules for battery storage sites. Operators must file thermal management plans before commissioning. Minimum separation distances from housing are specified. Existing sites have two years to comply."}
{"id": "sum-t08", "reference": "A courier moved inner-city deliveries to cargo bicycles, which beat traffic-delayed vans in the central zone, while vans still serve outer suburbs and heavy items.", "split": "test", "text": "A courier switched its inner-city deliveries to cargo bicycles. Vans were held up by traffic and parking restrictions. Bicycles completed the same routes faster in the central zone. Van use continues for outer suburbs and heavy items."}
